    "summary": "S5 FD-passing process handoff with identity state transfer (new binary).",
    "justification": [
      "goroutine-structure, long-running or start-up code changed: in-process patching would leave old code running in goroutines that never return; a new process starts the new goroutine structure, and the old one is drained and exits",
      "S6 blockers (14): github.com/gotify/server/v2.main: main() runs once at start-up (never re-executed / never returns); github.com/gotify/server/v2/api.ClientParams: layout of compiled-in type ClientParams changed (3 functions use it); S6 replaces functions, not types; github.com/gotify/server/v2/auth.Auth.handleClient: closures created before the patch (e.g. middleware chains built at start-up) keep the old code; only newly created closures see the fix; github.com/gotify/server/v2/auth.Database: interface method set changed (itabs and type assertions are compiled in); github.com/gotify/server/v2/router.Create: caller in the call-graph closure never returns; ... and 9 more"
    ],
    "alternatives": [
      "Kubernetes rolling update (loses in-memory state, needs surge capacity)"
    ],
    "risks": [
      "github.com/gotify/server/v2/database.GormDatabase.UpdateClientTokensLastUsed is exported: callers outside the analysed module are not in the closure",
      "github.com/gotify/server/v2/database.New is exported: callers outside the analysed module are not in the closure",
      "new package-level variable github.com/gotify/server/v2/test/testdb.Now: under S6 it lives in the patch plugin and is re-initialised by every later patch generation",
      "changed functions are small enough to be inlined; with S6 slot trampolines the call still dispatches through the slot, but raw binary patching (internal/livepatch) must also patch the inlining callers: github.com/gotify/server/v2/api.OIDCAPI.handleElevationCallback, github.com/gotify/server/v2/api.UserAPI.CreateUser, github.com/gotify/server/v2/api.UserAPI.GetUserByID, github.com/gotify/server/v2/api.UserAPI.GetUsers, github.com/gotify/server/v2/database.GormDatabase.DeleteUserByID, github.com/gotify/server/v2/test/testdb.AppClientBuilder.NewClientWithToken, github.com/gotify/server/v2/test/testdb.Database.AssertClientExist, github.com/gotify/server/v2/test/testdb.Database.AssertClientNotExist",
      "no patched function has a context.Context parameter: S6 gives per-call (not per-request) consistency, so one request may mix old and new versions of the 26 functions",
      "1 patched functions are in package main; a Go plugin cannot import package main, so hotpatchgen must relocate them into an importable package",
      "type information is partial (293/298 type errors old/new; third-party packages are opaque): call-graph and state reachability are lower bounds",
      "quiescence: old activations of main(), init-started or long-running goroutines never return, so the old process is retired by exit, not by draining; set a drain deadline in the S5 upgrader"
    ]
  },
